allwinner-i2c: the interrupt line follows INT_EN

The model raised the line when INT_FLAG was set with INT_EN on, and
lowered it only when INT_FLAG was cleared.  A handler that first turns
INT_EN off and clears the flag later -- the sun8iw19 (V831) vendor
Linux 4.9 i2c-sunxi.c does, writing the address byte from its
interrupt handler -- was entered again and again on the still-high
level and the CPU never left it.  The line is now INT_FLAG && INT_EN
after every CNTR write.

---
diff --git a/hw/i2c/allwinner-i2c.c b/hw/i2c/allwinner-i2c.c
index 1aa5493..d4e91ee 100644
--- a/hw/i2c/allwinner-i2c.c
+++ b/hw/i2c/allwinner-i2c.c
@@ -382,6 +382,9 @@ static void allwinner_i2c_write(void *opaque, hwaddr offset,
             }
             allwinner_i2c_raise_interrupt(s);
 
+            /* The line is INT_FLAG gated by INT_EN, both as just written. */
+            qemu_set_irq(s->irq, (s->cntr & TWI_CNTR_INT_FLAG) &&
+                                 allwinner_i2c_interrupt_is_enabled(s));
         }
         break;
     case TWI_CCR_REG:
